    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Hands-on Exercise 5b\"\nsubtitle: \"Building Ternary Plot with R\"\nauthor: \"Jedidiah Asaf T\"\nformat:\n  html:\n    toc: true\n    toc-depth: 3\n    code-fold: true\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nThis hands-on exercise recreates the key techniques from Chapter 13 of *R for Visual Analytics*. A **ternary plot** shows the composition of three mutually exclusive parts that sum to a whole. Here it is used to display the age structure (young / economically active / old) of Singapore's planning subzones, using `ggtern` for the static plot and `plotly` for the interactive version.\n\n## Setup\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nif (!require(pacman)) install.packages(\"pacman\")\n\npacman::p_load(plotly, ggtern, tidyverse)\n\npop_data <- read_csv(\"data/respopagsex2000to2018_tidy.csv\")\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Data Preparation\n\nThe tidy data is reshaped so each subzone becomes one row, then the age groups are aggregated into three classes: **YOUNG** (0-24), **ACTIVE** (25-64) and **OLD** (65+). Only the 2018 records with a positive population are kept.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nagpop_mutated <- pop_data %>%\n  mutate(Year = as.character(Year)) %>%\n  spread(AG, Population) %>%\n  mutate(YOUNG = rowSums(.[4:8])) %>%\n  mutate(ACTIVE = rowSums(.[9:16])) %>%\n  mutate(OLD = rowSums(.[17:21])) %>%\n  mutate(TOTAL = rowSums(.[22:24])) %>%\n  filter(Year == 2018) %>%\n  filter(TOTAL > 0)\n```\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nDT::datatable(\n  agpop_mutated %>% select(PA, SZ, YOUNG, ACTIVE, OLD, TOTAL),\n  class = \"compact\",\n  options = list(pageLength = 10, scrollX = TRUE)\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"datatables html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-650377b792c3fcb18b50\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-650377b792c3fcb18b50\">{\"x\":{\"filter\":\"none\",\"vertical\":false,\"data\":[[\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\",\"6